The plate is a square side plate, roughly 22 cm across. It holds two bacon pieces, one about 12 cm long and the other about 8 cm long. They look like cooked strips, and cooked bacon runs about 8 g per strip. The longer piece is nearly a full strip, and the shorter one is about half a strip. That gives roughly 1.5 strips, or about 12 g.

Cooked bacon is about 540 kcal per 100 g, so 12 g is about 65 kcal.

